From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: end the forward path at a device with tc

The forward path discovery walks from the route's device down to the
real device and offloads the flow there: the flowtable takes the
packets at the real device's ingress hook and transmits them on the
real device. A qdisc or a tc hook on a VLAN, PPPoE or bridge device in
between never sees the offloaded flow, so a shaper on such a device
stops shaping as soon as the flow is offloaded.

End the path at the first device, walking down from the route's
device, that has a root qdisc other than noqueue or noop, or a tcx/clsact
hook, and offload the flow at
that device. The flowtable then takes the packets after that device's
tc ingress, and transmits them through its qdisc. A flow whose path is
transmitted directly cannot end at a device that is not an Ethernet
device, so such a flow stays on the classic path.

nft_flowtable.sh gains a case with a pfifo qdisc and a tc ingress
filter on a VLAN device and on a bridge. Of a 2 MB transfer in each
direction, tc saw at most 352 bytes before this change, and all of it
after, for IPv4 and IPv6, with the flow offloaded in both cases.

Fixes: c63a7cc4d795 ("netfilter: flowtable: use dev_fill_forward_path() to obtain ingress device")
Fixes: 7a27f6ab4135 ("netfilter: flowtable: use dev_fill_forward_path() to obtain egress device")
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_core.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_extend.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_flow_table.h>
+#include <net/sch_generic.h>
 
 static enum flow_offload_xmit_type nft_xmit_type(struct dst_entry *dst)
 {
@@ -98,6 +99,19 @@ struct nft_forward_info {
 	enum flow_offload_xmit_type xmit_type;
 };
 
+/* A device with a qdisc or a tc hook must see the flow: the path ends there. */
+static bool nft_dev_has_tc(const struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	const struct Qdisc *q = rcu_dereference(dev->qdisc);
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_NET_XGRESS
+	if (rcu_access_pointer(dev->tcx_ingress) ||
+	    rcu_access_pointer(dev->tcx_egress))
+		return true;
+#endif
+	return q && q->enqueue && !(q->flags & TCQ_F_BUILTIN);
+}
+
 static int nft_dev_path_info(const struct net_device_path_stack *stack,
 			     struct nft_forward_info *info,
 			     unsigned char *ha, struct nf_flowtable *flowtable)
@@ -109,6 +123,17 @@ static int nft_dev_path_info(const struc
 
 	for (i = 0; i < stack->num_paths; i++) {
 		path = &stack->path[i];
+		if (i < stack->num_paths - 1 && nft_dev_has_tc(path->dev)) {
+			if (info->xmit_type == FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT &&
+			    !nft_is_valid_ether_device(path->dev))
+				return -1;
+
+			info->indev = path->dev;
+			if (is_zero_ether_addr(info->h_source))
+				memcpy(info->h_source, path->dev->dev_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+			break;
+		}
+
 		switch (path->type) {
 		case DEV_PATH_ETHERNET:
 		case DEV_PATH_IEEE80211:
